// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// VillainGroups File - defs/v_villaingroups_orig.def 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P3428670439" "Arachnos"
// Description :
"P2180492412" 		"Built upon the notion that only the fittest should survive, Arachnos was formed in the early part of the 20th Century in Italy. Although the true history of Arachnos remains shrouded, this organization was around long before "Il Recluso" wrested power away from its original founder, "The Weaver". It remains unclear exactly how Lord Recluse took over the global network of Arachnos, though betrayal and murder surely played a role. After taking over, Recluse subtly shifted Arachnos's priorities and interests to better suit his own ideological goals and now rules the Rogue isles from the center of his web of power."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P87788965" "Meteors"
// DisplaySingular :
"P685549473" "Meteor"
// Description :
"P1320768177" 		"Shiva was a massive asteroid that was headed directly toward Earth. A NASA scientist named it 'Shiva,' after the Hindu 'Destroyer of Worlds.' The meteor broke up over 20 years ago--some say thanks to a top-secret multinational project that cost five heroes their lives--but its remains, in the form of six meteors, struck the earth a short time ago."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P1614159436" "Shivans"
// DisplaySingular :
"P2509670649" "Shivan"
// Description :
"P1656192233" 		"Most citizens of Paragon City and the Rogue Isles recall the summer when the infamous meteor shower on Bloody Bay began. It wreaked havoc on the island, causing not only direct damage but radiation sickness and other, more sinister maladies as well. Perhaps strangest of all, weird energy from the meteor formed around the corpses of the dead and created protoplasmic entities filled with Shiva's destructive rage. Those few who know of Shiva wonder if these new creatures, the "Shivans", are somehow trying to reassemble the pieces and resurrect the Destroyer of Worlds. "

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P932482322" "Longbow"
// Description :
"P4287079172" 		"Organized by Ms. Liberty, the Longbow division of Freedom Corps is bent on the destruction of Arachnos. This militia extends its presence to every corner of the Rogue Isles, acting as a military support network for super-powered beings in the struggle against Lord Recluse. Drawing on those who want to be heroes, this organization is comprised of volunteers from around the world. Longbow thrives on the never-ending stream of idealistic youth who believe they are on the front lines in the battle against evil. "

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P3232244410" "Spectral Pirates"
// DisplaySingular :
"P21497369" "Spectral Pirate"
// Description :
"P2643364858" 		"As the sun sets over the bustling waters of Port Oakes, spectral forms slowly emerge from the shadows cast by the imposing walls of Fort Hades. Built by French occupiers in the 18th century, Hades was the scene of a brutal slaughter that forever marked this place as a vortex of terror. In the fateful year of 1718, a blood-thirsty pirate named Blackbeard sailed the seas surrounding these isles He put to shore at the fort and slaughtered all the soldiers there. To this day the souls of those murdered men haunt the area around Fort Hades, particularly at night."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P2606737056" "Mooks"
// DisplaySingular :
"P677511590" "Mook"
// Description :
"P762284296" 		"The Verandi family are small time hoods looking for a big score. Their head, Guido "The Mooch", is power hungry senses vulnerability in the Marcone family with the arrest of Manuel Marcone by Interpol. Guido and his Verandi mooks are trying to strike while the iron's hot and take over the Family operations for good."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P2017062408" "Coralax"
// Description :
"P113192538" 		"As the fetid swamps of the Earth's Cretaceous Period began to recede, the ancient godlike being Merulina crashed into the turbid waters of the expanding Atlantic. Settling into the ocean depths, the deity conjured followers, calling forth the Coralax from the incandescent coral thriving in the warm shallows. Made from coral imbued with Merulina's divine essence, the first Coralax were Shapers, high priests meant to lead the burgeoning Coralax civilization. Merulina fell into a deep sleep but the Coralax are slowly expanding their domain in preparation for the wakening of their god."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P4278007555" "Legacy Chain"
// Description :
"P1068761944" 		"Considered by some to be overly zealous, the Legacy Chain is perhaps the most secretive of all hero groups. Driven by an undying faith in the sanctity of magic, they willingly sacrifice their lives in their struggle against the dark arts. With ancient roots tracing back to the Old Ways of the Druids, these mystic soldiers seek to defeat anyone they believe defiles the purity of magic."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P1820908981" "Security Guards"
// DisplaySingular :
"P2639153458" "Security Guard"
// Description :
"P204352977" 		"It takes someone with fierce determination and a great deal of intestinal fortitude to accept a position as a security guard in a world filled with super-powered beings."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P876045537" "Freedom Phalanx"
// Description :
"P2809974497" 		"Founded by Statesman and other heroes in 1932, the premiere hero team in Paragon City is hated and feared by villains all over the world and beyond. If you find yourself up against a member of the Freedom Phalanx, you've hit the big time."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P388995295" "Wyvern"
// Description :
"P4211143061" 		"According to public record, Wyvern is a private security agency hired by Paragon's wealthiest families. Yet the public face, upheld by owner Delia Huntley, masks the true nature of this dangerous strike force. Behind the facade, Wyvern is in fact the dark arm of Manticore's crusade for justice. Justin Sinclair, aka Manticore, was increasingly frustrated by the limitations placed upon the heroes of Paragon City, and so he created Wyvern to carry out those ambiguous tasks that the Freedom Corps is unwilling to perform. Firm believers in the notion that the ends justify the means, Wyvern agents walk the line between hero and mercenary. "

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P438858934" "Siren's Call Phantom"
// Description :
"P415750680" 		"These creatures are vicious spirits drawn to Siren's Call by a supernatural vortex."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P698968999" "Snakes"
// DisplaySingular :
"P1671704095" "Snake"
// Description :
"P1261033661" 		"Very little is known about the origins of the Snakes that now swarm Mercy Island. Rumors abound that they are the legacy of the esoteric Mu while others believe that they are somehow linked to the Children of Enos, the mystic cult that once dominated these isles. Though their antiquity coupled with their humanoid features suggest that their provenience can be found in the realm of the arcane, further study has revealed that their actual origin is linked to neither of these ancient groups. They are actually born of Stheno the Gorgon, sister of Medusa."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P9422944" "Cap au Diable Demons"
// DisplaySingular :
"P2630775142" "Cap au Diable Demon"
// Description :
"P1437017407" 		"These terrible little monsters somehow live inside the Cap au Diable Power Transference System. There is more to the 'PTS' than meets the eye. Many wonder why the PTS is covered in glowing sigils. Those mystical markings are the only thing keeping these demons in check at all."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P1489618071" "Mastermind Pet"
// DisplaySingular :
"P3404795231" "Mastermind Pets"
// Description :
"P2522879592" 		"The walking dead, robots, and Ninja are only a few of the trusty servants to be found in this category."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P1082918703" "Scrapyarders"
// DisplaySingular :
"P1074419852" "Scrapyarder"
// Description :
"P894630529" 		"This heroic group is currently led by the Iron Widow and her lieutenant, Spinnerette. They have continued fighting the good fight that was begun by their leader, the Scrapyarder, who was killed by Captain Mako. Although they lose many battles, they're still hoping to win their war against the Cage Consortium and the other villains of Sharkhead Isle."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P2338688493" "Slag Golems"
// DisplaySingular :
"P3358791228" "Slag Golem"
// Description :
"P692244353" 		"The Slag Golems are terrifying monstrosities of living cast-off metal, shambling figures composed of crudely sentient dross and detritus, eager to pound anyone who crosses them into compost for the island. The Slag Golems constantly speak of protecting a Guardian, and suggest that human presence, specifically digging down into Sharkhead, threatens or harms the Guardian. They have only one response to those they perceive as a danger to the Guardian - direct violence. This guardian is tied to the powerful and mysterious red coral that surrounds Sharkhead and their are many groups around the Rogue Isles trying to unlock its secrets."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P2452440701" "Gold Brickers"
// DisplaySingular :
"P3972986794" "Gold Bricker"
// Description :
"P2009502361" 		"A glimpse into the shadows cast by Aeon City's gleaming white towers reveals a dangerous nexus of chaos lurking in the darkest nooks of this seemingly safe area. Harnessing this thinly veiled chaos, the shadowy King Midas and his notorious gang of thieves, the Gold Brickers, maintain a firm grip on the urban crime of Aeon City. Monitoring the city from the highest rooftops, the Gold Brickers are no common street criminals. These high-tech thieves rely on unparalleled technological equipment and brazen aggression to target only the wealthiest of Aeon City. Able to make quick escapes with their jetpacks, the Gold Brickers have taken the heist to new levels of profitability, fulfilling rumors that any caper coordinated by King Midas does indeed turn to gold."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P2008658219" "Luddites"
// DisplaySingular :
"P2911349863" "Luddite"
// Description :
"P3124649903" 		"Predisposed to distrust technology of any kind, the futuristic technological advances brought to Cap au Diable by Dr. Aeon have sent the Luddites into a frenzy. Originally a ragtag band of unorganized activists, the Luddites have coalesced around a cause, prompted by the construction of Dr. Aeon's Power Transfer System. Convinced that all advanced technologies are dangerous, the superstitious Luddites believe that the PTS actually draws its energy from a demon entombed in Mount Diable." 

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P3253344005" "Wailers"
// DisplaySingular :
"P2550972248" "Wailer"
// Description :
"P1208585599" 		"The Wailers are demons infesting St. Martial with powerful sonic attacks. Johnny Sonata made a pact with these demons: selling his soul for fame and influence. Now, the terms have reached their time of fulfillment and the Wailers have come to collect Johnny's life. After becoming a star singer, Johnny had mystic obelisks erected around the Golden Giza to ward the demons from the entire island. They are intent on collecting their due, however, and have become very violent in their efforts to capture their end of the deal."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P916332205" "Arachnoids"
// DisplaySingular :
"P2387757772" "Arachnoid"
// Description :
"P1168636299" 		"Created during Project Fury, this group consists of former Arachnos soldiers injected with the drug Venom, which itself is a synthesis of Lord Recluse's blood. The results were only partially successful, resulting in creatures who are incredibly strong but monstrous. These pitiful wretches have had their vocal cords removed to help keep the secret of their origin safe and serve Arachnos as foot soldiers."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P646235446" "Generic Heroes"
// DisplaySingular :
"P282765013" "Generic Hero"
// Description :
"P1358888645" 		"Since the brutal losses during the Rikti War, more heroes appear on the scene every day. Their origins, powers, and crusades are as varied as imagination itself."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P137753798" "Cage Consortium Guards"
// DisplaySingular :
"P1271921195" "Cage Consortium Guard"
// Description :
"P734488821" 		"Working for the Cage Consortium is a very small step up from a security job anywhere else on the Rogue Isles. You gain a smaller set of enemies at the cost of working for one of the most oppressive groups around."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P252676002" "Infected"
// Description :
"P3926367423" 		"The cesspool on Mercy Island became the only source of drinkable water over a year ago. Those who are forced to use it to survive, slowly devolve into mindless creatures with	frightening strength. Perhaps even more chilling is the recent evidence that the condition can be spread and cases have been reported in Paragon City. In addition, rumors persist that in very rare cases the infected can manifest other powers and even retain their intelligence."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P1169852419" "Rogue Arachnos"
// Description :
"P716062260" 		"Led by Marshal Blitz and headquartered in Warburg, these rogue agents chafe at the slow and quiet approach Lord Recluse has taken to world domination. They are in favor of launching the Warburg rockets and showing the world in one white-hot instant that Arachnos are the true and proper rulers of the human race."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P950225890" "Spetsnaz Commandos"
// DisplaySingular :
"P1754216388" "Spetsnaz Commando"
// Description :
"P1445783010" 		"This elite military unit has been honed by Dmitri Krylov into a deadly fighting force."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P3060434880" "Miscellaneous"
// Description :
"P4109406819" 		"Villains, agents, and even an insidious boom box can be found in this group."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P3043642532" "Vindicators"
// DisplaySingular :
"P2844099803" "Vindicator"
// Description :
"P4173861431" 		"This group was formed by Ms. Liberty to aid redeemed villains, dark heroes, and visitors from other dimensions. Filled with outcasts and misfits, it has become a dynamic force for unity in Paragon City and shows what good can come from second chances."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P92774587" "Bat'Zul"
// Description :
"P1909103276" 		"A demon-lord of the lowest planes of existence, Bat'Zul's immense power has been shackled beneath Cap au Diable for hundreds of years. Should he escape, he could turn all of the Rogue Isles into an inferno of destruction. His servitors are legion and manifest on the surface of the island to do his bidding."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P3992977855" "Paragon Heroes"
// DisplaySingular :
"P910205991" "Paragon Hero"
// Description :
"P3945648556" 		"The heroes of Paragon City stand ready to prevent mayhem, the primary mission of many villains who reside on the Rogue Isles."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P2083337618" "Rogue Island Police"
// Description :
"P2977095254" 		"Lord Recluse knows that any villain hoping to keep his public image shiny needs to have a legal police force. Of course the RIP's real motto is 'To pummel and subdue'."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P828729482" "Dockworkers"
// DisplaySingular :
"P417363144" "Dockworker"
// Description :
"P3373699992" 		"Everyone knows you don't mess with a union man."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P4177809194" "Paragon Police"
// Description :
"P2879663548" 		"No amount of high tech gadgetry or super-powered support can replace the fundamental quality needed to serve with the blue shield...the heart of a lion."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P2457047361" "W.I.S.D.O.M."
// Description :
"P3765811165" 		"Led by Foreshadow, this group of heroes protects all of Asia. They met Statesman on one of his many journeys around the world and have been seen upon occasion in Paragon City and the Rogue Isles, lending a hand to their old comrade."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P3284501742" "Generic Villains"
// DisplaySingular :
"P3658243739" "Generic Villain"
// Description :
"P3372257252" 		"These villains have no allies, only enemies." 

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P817996952" "Rogue Isles Villains"
// DisplaySingular :
"P1734172809" "Rogue Isles Villain"
// Description :
"P1621895890" 		"These dastardly miscreants make Safeguarding Paragon City the ultimate challenge."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P2677346818" "Peacebringers"
// DisplaySingular :
"P972076576" "Peacebringer"
// Description :
"P1433807880" 		"These Kheldians only merge with those who are willing and tend to choose members of law enforcement or other forces for justice in the world as their new hosts."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// Description :
"P3832759211" 		"Although Arachnos has only come to attention on the world stage in the last decade, they have been around for far longer than that spinning their insidious web."

// ////////////////////////////////////////////////////// 
// DisplayName :
"P425589940" "Pandora's Might"
// Description :
"P2172191412" 		"These violent creatures appear to be manifestations of the power released from Pandora's Box. Why they have taken form themselves, rather than claiming a host, you cannot say."
